## Approval

- [ ] Active patterns are listed (which of the 5 patterns)
- [ ] Per-tier permission matrix is filled in
- [ ] Tool-call budget per pattern is set
- [ ] On-demand context budget per load strategy is set
- [ ] Concurrent-write strategy is chosen
- [ ] Approved scaffold patterns are listed
- [ ] Archivist triggers are listed (4 evidence-based)
- [ ] Audit-line format is documented
- [ ] The 5-question interaction audit is scheduled quarterly

Once all 9 boxes are checked, the agent vault permissions are ready.

---

## How the friend uses this template

1. **List your agents.** (The friend has 1 default + 2-4 named agents.)
2. **Fill in the permissions for each agent.** Start with Read-only + Propose as defaults.
3. **Tune the per-tier matrix.** Each agent's role determines which tiers it can edit.
4. **Set the tool-call budget.** Start with defaults; adjust based on actual usage.
5. **List the approved scaffold patterns.** New patterns are operator-actionable.
6. **Set the archive triggers.** The 4 evidence-based triggers only.
7. **Schedule the quarterly interaction audit.** Use the 5-question audit.

The agent vault permissions are operator-context. The friend running Alice's methodology designs their own permissions for their own agents — they apply the method to derive their own, not to copy the operator's specific choices.